  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1127 AM CDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\nHurricane Isaias is forecast to make landfall along the Gulf Coast\ntomorrow, dissipating as it moves NNW. Shower and thunderstorm\nchances will increase from south to north early Saturday and peak\nSaturday afternoon through Saturday night. This tropical system\nwill bring an abundance of moisture, likely producing 1-3\" of \nrain across the area (highest south of I-40). Although we need the\nrain given the ongoing moderate to extreme drought across Middle\nTN, our prolonged dry conditions will reduce the soil's ability to\nabsorb water and will increase our chances for flash flooding. \nTherefore, a Flood Watch is in effect for portions of Middle TN\nfrom late Friday night through Sunday morning.\n\nWind gusts up to 30-40 mph are expected and a few brief spin-up \ntornadoes are possible Saturday afternoon and Saturday night.\nTropical tornadoes can form and dissipate quickly and can develop\nfrom weak showers or storms.\n\nConditions will improve through the day on Sunday with the last of\nthe rain clearing the area by Sunday night. \n\nAt the start of next week, warm and dry conditions will return\nwith daily highs in the 80s and overnight lows in the 50s and 60s.",
